# CourtLive — Global Rules

## Project Context
UCSD ECE 196 engineering project. ESP32 PCB with PIR sensor detects court
occupancy and sends data to a hosted API. A public dashboard shows live status.

## Stack
- Backend:  Node.js + Express + TypeScript, deployed on Render (free tier)
- Database: Turso (SQLite via libSQL) — NOT MySQL
- Frontend: React + Vite + TypeScript, deployed on Vercel via CLI
- Firmware: Arduino C++ on ESP32 via PlatformIO

## Critical Constants
- ESP32 polls every 300 seconds (5 minutes)
- Occupancy expires 10 minutes after last occupied ping
- Sensor marked offline if updated_at > 12 minutes old
- Court hours: Mon-Fri 7am-11pm, Sat-Sun 8am-10pm (America/Los_Angeles)
- getSleepSeconds() returns 300 during hours, seconds-until-open outside (cap 3600)

## SQLite Rules (Turso uses SQLite, NOT MySQL)
- Use INTEGER (0 or 1) for booleans — never BOOLEAN
- Use TEXT in ISO 8601 format for timestamps — never DATETIME or NOW()
- Compute expiry in JavaScript: new Date(Date.now() + ms).toISOString()
- Upsert syntax: ON CONFLICT(col) DO UPDATE SET ... — never ON DUPLICATE KEY
- db.execute() takes { sql: string, args: any[] } — never positional mysql2 style

## Production Domains (ethanha.com — not courtlive.com)
- Dashboard (Vercel): https://ethanha.com
- API (Render custom domain): https://api.ethanha.com
- UptimeRobot / firmware target: https://api.ethanha.com/ping and /api/reading

## Environment Variables (never hardcode these)
Backend:  TURSO_URL, TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN, DEVICE_API_KEY, FRONTEND_URL (https://ethanha.com in prod), PORT
Frontend: VITE_API_URL (https://api.ethanha.com in prod)
Firmware: defined as #define constants in main.cpp (filled before flashing)

## Code Style
- TypeScript strict mode everywhere (frontend + backend)
- No default exports in hooks or utility files — named exports only
- No external UI component libraries (no shadcn, MUI, Chakra, etc.)
- CSS: inline styles or a single <style> block — no CSS modules, no Tailwind
- Every async function must have try/catch with a meaningful error message
- Never use console.log in production paths — use console.error for errors only
